<!--
  Chapter 58 — CI/CD, GitOps & Progressive Delivery.
    gitops/     Inventory (what a controller owns, and what to prune) and Reconciler (fetch, render, server-side
                apply, revert drift, prune: the loop Argo CD and Flux run)
    delivery/   CanaryAnalysis (promote, wait or abort from per-version error rates and latency)
    resources/  gitops/menu-prod (an environment repository's view of a service), delivery/ (Traefik's Gateway API
                provider, a weighted HTTPRoute), ci/pipeline.yaml (build once, sign, open a pull request)
  verify/run.sh runs the reconciler against a Git repository and a real cluster (k3s 1.37 with Traefik 3.7):
  commits, drift, deletions and pruning; canaries through HTTPRoute weights against a rolling update; and a
  blue/green switch under new-connection and keep-alive load.
-->
